<%#
  Kaminari's pagination. The <nav> and its label live here rather than at the call site,
  because three views call `paginate` directly and would otherwise ship an unlabelled list.

  Prev and Next are always drawn, disabled when they lead nowhere, so the control set does not
  change width as you page -- it used to be 7 controls on page 1, 14 on page 5 and 8 on the
  last page, which moves the buttons under the cursor of the person using them.

  First and Last are the exception: on a table that fits on one page they do not mean anything
  at all, so they are not drawn. On a longer table they are, disabled at the ends.
%>
<%= paginator.render do %>
  <nav aria-label="Pagination">
    <ul class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1">
      <%= first_page_tag if total_pages > 1 %>
      <%= prev_page_tag %>
      <% each_page do |page| %>
        <% if page.left_outer? || page.right_outer? || page.inside_window? %>
          <%= page_tag page %>
        <% elsif !page.was_truncated? -%>
          <%= gap_tag %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
      <%= next_page_tag %>
      <%= last_page_tag if total_pages > 1 %>
    </ul>
  </nav>
<% end %>
